  "name": "LATO.2 — image/mesh to 3D mesh with controllable vertex count (code + weights)",
  "summary": "Open research model that generates a 3D mesh in two stages: vertex positions under a vertex budget you choose (V-Flow), then the connectivity (T-Flow). Works from an input mesh (remesh/retopology) or, since Nov 19, from a single image via a TRELLIS scaffold. Updated v1.0+rl weights (Nov 18) clean up topology. Useful for game-ready low/mid-poly meshes with a set polycount. Needs an NVIDIA GPU with CUDA.",
  "category": "models-weights",
